    "etymology": {
     "text": "From Proto-West Semitic *laban-; cognate with Arabic لَبَن (laban, “milk”), Ugaritic lbn and Phoenician lbn (Wiktionary). Root ל־ב־ן, pattern קָטָל.",
     "src": "Wiktionary (kaikki.org)"
    },
    "funFacts": [
     "Arabic لَبَن is “milk” — the white drink; and לְבָנוֹן, Lebanon, is named for its white, snowy mountains."
    ],
    "pitfalls": [
     "The first vowel shortens: לְבָנָה, לְבָנִים.",
     "The feminine לְבָנָה is also a poetic word for the moon, and לְבֵנָה (with e) is a brick."
    ],
    "subtleties": [
     "Blue and white are the colours of the flag: תּוֹצֶרֶת כָּחֹל לָבָן “blue-and-white made” means “made in Israel”."
    ]
